From 1a95125ff0ebe788993f98f8d9fff29b9edf49fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: utzcoz <utzcoz@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 21:05:28 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/7] webxr: add XRSession.trackedSources and
 XRInputSource.skipRendering

Implement both behind WebXRSpecParity.

trackedSources lists the input sources without a primary action, which
devices already mark as auxiliary. They are only reported to sessions
that request the new "tracked-sources" feature, and fire
trackedsourceschange instead of inputsourceschange. A source that gains
or loses its primary action moves between the two lists as a new
XRInputSource. OpenXR sessions support the feature. ARCore does not
yet, so with the flag on its auxiliary sources leave inputSources.

skipRendering is true when the display is see-through, where the user
already sees their real controllers and hands.

Bug: 506004811
Change-Id: I095380b06df462f85d468ec397fdb8b8861e426a
